.TH EYE 1 "August 2026" "Agent Eye 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
eye \- run, deduplicate, observe, and safely stop host or Docker tasks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eye doc
.br
.B eye npu_status
.br
.B eye run
[--container NAME] --exec COMMAND [--tag TAG] [--detach] [--log FILE]
.br
.B eye ensure
[--container NAME] --tag TAG --exec COMMAND [--detach] [--log FILE]
.br
.B eye kill
[--container NAME] --tag TAG
.br
.B eye from_file
FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Agent Eye is a zero-third-party-dependency Python command-line tool for querying NPU
state and managing commands on the host or in Docker containers.
.PP
For the canonical, detailed guide run
.BR "eye doc" .
The guide is read directly from the installed source tree, so it includes complete
examples, JSON schemas, scheduling rules, output semantics, safety boundaries, and
troubleshooting notes.
.SH QUICK START FOR AGENTS
Use
.B run
for one unconditional execution. Use
.B ensure
when a stable tag must not be started twice. Prefer the following pattern for a
long-running host task:
.PP
.nf
eye ensure \\
  --tag my-unique-task --detach \\
  --log /tmp/my-unique-task.log \\
  --exec "python3 /absolute/path/to/task.py"
.fi
.PP
Omitting the container option executes on the host. Add
.B --container NAME
to execute in Docker. In container mode, command and log paths refer to the
container. Do not put nohup or & in --exec; use --detach.
.SH COMMAND SELECTION
.TP
.B npu_status
Run npu-smi info and print one four-column row per device:
.PP
.nf
0,FREE,null,null
1,PROCESSING,VLLM,z50064016
2,PROCESSING,VLLM,null
.fi
.PP
The columns are NPU ID, status, process type, and owner ID. For every process PID,
eye follows the full ps parent chain to ppid=0 and searches each command for a path
component matching one letter plus eight digits, such as /z50064016/. Missing,
vanished, cyclic, or conflicting ownership is reported as null.
.TP
.B run
Always execute one command. It blocks by default and returns the real command status.
.TP
.B ensure
Check a literal tag and execute only when no matching task exists. Concurrent calls
are protected by a non-blocking host lock.
.TP
.B kill
Safely stop the one task matching a tag. It fails closed on ambiguous matches,
unreadable process state, UID mismatch, or protected processes.
.TP
.B from_file
Execute one JSON task description.
.TP
.B doc
Print the complete Markdown user and agent guide to standard output.
.TP
.B test
Run repository JSON scenarios and Python tests.
.SH STATUS CONTRACT
.TP
.B SUCCEEDED
A blocking command completed successfully.
.TP
.B FAILED
Startup, inspection, or command execution failed. Read stderr and the task log.
.TP
.B STARTED
A detached command was submitted. This does not mean the task ultimately succeeded;
inspect its log later.
.TP
.B SKIPPED
No action was needed or allowed. A skipped ensure with mode, tag, and PID means the
tagged task already exists. Explicit reasons include ensure_in_progress,
tag_not_found, and outside_allow.
.TP
.B KILLED
The unique matching process tree passed safety review and received SIGTERM.
.SH TIME WINDOWS
The global
.B --allow WINDOW
gate is checked before external queries or execution. Example:
.PP
.nf
eye --allow "workday:0900-1200,1300-1800" npu_status
.fi
.PP
Use four-digit local HHMM times. Ranges include both endpoints. Split ranges that
cross midnight, for example 2200-2359,0000-0600.
.SH FILE TASKS
A detached local ensure task can be written as:
.PP
.nf
{
  "command": "ensure",
  "tag": "training-01",
  "exec": "python3 /workspace/train.py",
  "detach": true,
  "log": "/tmp/training-01.log"
}
.fi
.PP
Run it with
.BR "eye from_file /absolute/path/to/task.json" .
.SH SAFETY
The --exec value is a complete shell command and must be trusted. Host commands run
with the invoking user's privileges. Use stable, unique, literal tags. STARTED only
confirms submission. Local safe kill needs readable Linux /proc and is unavailable
on default macOS. Container kill requires readable /proc inside the container.
.SH DOCUMENTATION
Run
.B eye doc
for the full guide. Run
.B eye help COMMAND
for concise argument help.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
.BR crontab (5),
.BR pgrep (1)
